  "body": "I use the following query to sync with matrix.org\r\n\r\n```json\r\nsync?full_state=true&set_presence=online&filter={\"presence\":{\"limit\":0},\"room\":{\"ephemeral\":{\"limit\":0},\"timeline\":{\"limit\":70}}}\r\n```\r\nbut I receive an empty `state` array on the rooms which I am the creator. \r\n\r\nIf I remove the timeline filter like so\r\n\r\n```json\r\nsync?full_state=true&set_presence=online&filter={\"presence\":{\"limit\":0},\"room\":{\"ephemeral\":{\"limit\":0}}}\r\n```\r\nI receive all the `state` arrays as expected. \r\n\r\nIs this the expected behavior? The spec states that if `full_state: true` all the state events will be returned. Also it seems really unintuitive that a timeline filter will affected the state.",
